# im an obsessive learner — for domain invariants 🦉📜

zoom-in of `im_an.obsessive_learner`: *what must always hold true in this domain*. lands in `define.invariant.<scope>.md`. peer of `.for.domain.terms`.

## label the KIND first

| kind | holds because | overturn by proof that |
|---|---|---|
| nature | of what the domain is | the domain was misread (not *"inconvenient"*) |
| nurture | we chose it, paid in incidents | incidents no longer apply or cost changed (not *"i'd choose differently"*) |

nature: *a machine is never blank*, so `upgrade` is accurate, `install` misleads. nurture: *one entrypoint*.

## the shape

1. **.what** — rule, one line, imperative
2. **.kind** — nature|nurture + why
3. **.invariant** — formal (`A ⟺ B`)
4. **.why** — what depends on it; often an incident
5. **.scope** — what it does NOT cover
6. **.the litigation** — what was argued and what settled it, in your own words; never quote the wisher or cite their seed (`rule.forbid.verbatim-quotes-outside-seeds`)
7. **.the counter-argument** — strongest case against, fairly
8. **.what would overturn it**
9. **.enforcement**

a settled invariant is NOT deferrable: it gets its brief this round. defer only a rule still disputed or that wants deeper discovery.
